[3.X] Add Form Tabs support #4725

### Add feature to support form tabs on cruds

I've found a rapid way to make it works.
What do you think about it ?

Example of how to use this feature

_

In pages where you display lots of fields, you can divide them in tabs using
the "tabs" created with the special FormField object::

use EasyCorp\Bundle\EasyAdminBundle\Field\FormField;

public function configureFields(string $pageName): iterable
{
    return [
        IdField::new('id')->hideOnForm(),

        // Add a tab
        FormField::addTab('First Tab'),

        // You can use a Form Panel inside a Form Tab
        FormField::addPanel('User Details'),

        // Your fields
        TextField::new('firstName'),
        TextField::new('lastName'),

        // Add a second Form Tab
        // Tabs can also define their icon, CSS class and help message
        FormField::addPanel('Contact information')
            ->setIcon('phone')->addCssClass('optional')
            ->setHelp('Phone number is preferred'),
        FormField::addPanel('Second Tab'),

        TextField::new('phone'),

    ];
}
_

### Issue

Currently every generated fields in the schema is nullable, even though the field was marked as required.

```
type CustomType {
  title: String
}
```

With this PR it checks the `required` or/and the `allow_null` property and generates the schema properly.

```
type CustomType {
  title: String!
}
```

### Motivation
When using the schema to generate types (eg. for TypeScript), every type is nullable, which makes it unusable with the `strict` option in TypeScript.

This is the result from the generated type:
```
interface CustomType {
  title: string | null;
}
```

