Added support the the "k6" load testing tool.
Added `k6-script.js` to test EACH endpoint and ensure latency < 2000ms.
Created a Postman Collection for test each endpoint's response code and latency.
Tested URLs for data in last 10 of data set.

[Article](https://medium.com/@gururajhm/load-testing-api-with-postman-node-js-k6-8fa04725e3b4)
```js
// In Postman
METHOD: GET http://localhost:3000/products/

// Tests tab
pm.test("Status code is 200", function () {
  pm.response.to.have.status(200);
});

pm.test("Response time is less than 2000ms", () => {
  pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(2000);
});
```

```sh
* Create Postman collection *
* Export Postman collection to .json file*
$ npm install -g postman-to-k6
$ postman-to-k6 Capsules_Testpostman_collection.json — iterations 25 -o k6-script.js
$ k6 run k6-script.js
$ k6 login cloud --token <YOUR_K6_TOKEN>
$ k6 cloud k6-script.js
```

